{
  "info": {
    "name": "FairSpot meetups",
    "description": "Test requests for /api/meetups and voting (FairSpot, IS216 G9T6). Start the server first: cd server && pnpm dev.\n\nBefore you start, log in (POST /api/users/login) and paste the sessionToken into the collection variable \"sessionToken\". Then run the requests in order: \"Create meetup\" saves the new meetup code in \"code\", and \"Join meetup as a guest\" saves the guest's secret in \"memberToken\".\n\nWho \"me\" is: the server never takes a member id from the URL or body. A logged-in member sends Authorization: Bearer <sessionToken>; a guest sends X-Member-Token: <memberToken>.\n\nTest inputs written with AI assistance (allowed: test cases and sample inputs).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000/api",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "code",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "memberToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Create meetup (logged in)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 201', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('response has a meetup code and the host\\'s memberToken', function () {",
              "  const meetup = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(meetup.code).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.expect(meetup.memberToken).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('code', meetup.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('no member carries a memberToken', function () {",
              "  pm.response.json().members.forEach(function (member) {",
              "    pm.expect(member).to.not.have.property('memberToken');",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{sessionToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/meetups",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "meetups"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Needs a login: paste a session token from POST /api/users/login into the \"sessionToken\" variable first. Expect 201 and the saved meetup with the host's memberToken (sent only this once). Saves its code in the \"code\" variable.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"occasion\": \"Friday dinner\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-11-20\",\n  \"time\": \"18:00\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Create meetup, missing field (expect 400)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 400', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('response has an error message', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{sessionToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/meetups",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "meetups"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The body has no \"time\". Expect 400 and { error: \"...\" }.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"occasion\": \"Friday dinner\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-11-20\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Join meetup as a guest",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 201', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('response is the new member with an _id and a memberToken', function () {",
              "  const member = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(member._id).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.expect(member.name).to.eql('Bea');",
              "  pm.expect(member.memberToken).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('memberToken', member.memberToken);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/meetups/{{code}}/members",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "meetups",
            "{{code}}",
            "members"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Expect 201 and the new member { _id, name, start: null, memberToken }. Saves the memberToken in the \"memberToken\" variable: it is the guest's secret, and the server only sends it this once.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Bea\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Set my start (guest)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('my start point is saved', function () {",
              "  const member = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(member.name).to.eql('Bea');",
              "  pm.expect(member.start.lat).to.eql(1.3562);",
              "  pm.expect(member).to.not.have.property('memberToken');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-Member-Token",
            "value": "{{memberToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/meetups/{{code}}/me",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "meetups",
            "{{code}}",
            "me"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The server works out which member \"me\" is from X-Member-Token (or a login session). Expect 200 and the updated member, without its memberToken.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"start\": {\n    \"label\": \"Tampines MRT\",\n    \"postal\": \"529538\",\n    \"lat\": 1.3562,\n    \"lng\": 103.9546\n  }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Set start, no credential (expect 403)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 403', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('response has an error message', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/meetups/{{code}}/me",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "meetups",
            "{{code}}",
            "me"
          ]
        },
        "description": "No session and no X-Member-Token, so the server can't tell which member this is. Expect 403 { error: \"You are not a member of this meetup.\" }.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"start\": {\n    \"label\": \"Tampines MRT\",\n    \"postal\": \"529538\",\n    \"lat\": 1.3562,\n    \"lng\": 103.9546\n  }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Get meetup (no credential)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('meetup has the requested code', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('code'));",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('no memberToken and no start coordinates', function () {",
              "  pm.response.json().members.forEach(function (member) {",
              "    pm.expect(member).to.not.have.property('memberToken');",
              "    if (member.start) {",
              "      pm.expect(member.start).to.have.property('label');",
              "      pm.expect(member.start).to.not.have.property('lat');",
              "      pm.expect(member.start).to.not.have.property('postal');",
              "    }",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/meetups/{{code}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "meetups",
            "{{code}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Anyone with the code can read it. Expect 200, no memberToken anywhere, and start points as their label only."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Get meetup as a member",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('start points have lat/lng, and no memberToken', function () {",
              "  const bea = pm.response.json().members.find(function (member) { return member.name === 'Bea'; });",
              "  pm.expect(bea.start.lat).to.eql(1.3562);",
              "  pm.expect(bea).to.not.have.property('memberToken');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Member-Token",
            "value": "{{memberToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/meetups/{{code}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "meetups",
            "{{code}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "With a member's credential the start points also have postal and lat/lng (the results map shows them to members). Still no memberToken."
      },
      "response": []
    },
